   "subject": "Spatiotemporal data: indexing question",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hello,</div><div><br></div><div>I am modeling a moderate-sized dataset (3108*14) using a spatiotemporal hierarchical model.</div><div>Until now, I used the temporal index first then spatial index afterwards. After reading other threads in this board, I realized that the index &#39;should&#39; be in spatial-temporal order. For example,</div><div></div><div>My data have had space-time indices as below (in case of spacedim=3, timelength=3)<br></div><div>space  time</div><div>1         1</div><div>1         2</div><div>1         3</div><div>2         1</div><div>2         2</div><div>2         3</div><div>3         1</div><div>3         2</div><div>3         3</div><div><br></div><div>But after referring to the answer for the other thread, the indices should have had:</div><div>space  time</div><div>1         1</div><div>2         1</div><div>3         1</div><div>1         2</div><div>2         2</div><div>3         2</div><div>1         3</div><div>2         3</div><div>3         3</div><div><br></div><div>Thus, my questions would be: 1) I am curious if my modeling was wrong for now. I wonder if the INLA algorithm automatically sort the results by its space-time indices by referring the column names defined in the f() function.</div><div>For your reference, my formula was</div><br><div style=\"color:#d4d4d4;background-color:#1e1e1e;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;font-weight:normal;font-size:14px;line-height:19px;white-space:pre\"><div><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">form.m42 &lt;- Mortrate </span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">~</span><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\"> </span></div><div><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">  f(GEOID, model = </span><span style=\"color:#ce9178\">&quot;bym&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">, graph = graph, constr = </span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">, hyper = hyp.prior) +</span></div><div><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">  f(year1, model = </span><span style=\"color:#ce9178\">&#39;ar1&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">, constr = </span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">) +</span></div><div><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">  f(GEOID1, UELAG1, model = </span><span style=\"color:#ce9178\">&quot;bym&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">, graph = graph, constr = </span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">, hyper = hyp.prior) +</span></div><div><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">  f(year2, UELAG1, model = </span><span style=\"color:#ce9178\">&#39;ar1&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">, constr = </span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">) +</span></div><div><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">  f(GEOID2, UELAG1, model = </span><span style=\"color:#ce9178\">&quot;bym&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">, graph = graph, group = year3, control.group = </span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">list</span><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">(model = </span><span style=\"color:#ce9178\">&quot;rw1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">),</span></div><div><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">    constr = </span><span style=\"color:#569cd6\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">, hyper = hyp.prior) + </span></div><div><span style=\"color:#d4d4d4\">  PELDER + PNONWHITE + MEDINCOME + PUNIVABOVE + PPOVTBELOW + PRURAL + PRENTER + PHSINGLE</span></div><br><br></div><div>In this case, 2) I want to know the INLA model using form.m42 will automatically sort the output by GEOID2 and year3 or others (e.g. GEOID1, year2, etc.).<br></div><div><br></div><div>Thank you.<br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "9pVasXgDBAAJ",
