   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div>your results are probably ok; if you&#39;ve been looking at the linear.predictor or fitted.values output, they will have been in the order that your index vectors were specified.</div><div>The only issue would be if you also looked at the individual random effect results separately, since they will have been stored in the second type of order (with space index varying fastest, and the time index varying slowly).</div><div><br></div><div>Finn</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thu, 22 Oct 2020 at 21:46, Insang Song &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">sigma...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
