   "subject": "Re: [r-inla] Spatiotemporal data: indexing question",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>the two recent threads</div><div>  &quot;using whole linear predictor of one variable as part of linear predictor of other variable&quot;</div><div>and</div><div>  &quot;Copying a part of the linear predictor&quot;</div><div>sounds like what you may be looking for.</div><div>Can you write the desired model in more mathematical form? E.g. if your model should take the form covariate(s) * (beta0 + field(s)), or if it&#39;s something else you&#39;re looking for?<br>The code alone doesn&#39;t tell us what model you&#39;re looking for; One can only see if it&#39;s correct if it can be compared with a well-formulated model definition.</div><div><br></div><div>Finn</div><div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Sun, 25 Oct 2020 at 17:23, Insang Song &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">sigma...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
